# WARP-8: HOME on the kit writes steps. A black key picks the drum, a white key is its step (a tap toggles; held,
# the knobs are the step's); a black key held, the knobs shape its lane; OCT is the bar. HOME held, the white keys
# are the scenes, and the page stays
wait 300
listen
expect trk 1
tap HOME
wait 40
expect page Arrange
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w4
wait 40
said step 5 on
# (the pick's audition, then steps 1 and 5)
tap PLAY
wait 1900
tap PLAY
expect drumhits 3
# a step held: knob 1 its velocity
key w4 down
wait 100
turn K1 -40
wait 40
key w4 up
wait 40
expect stepvel 1 1 5 60
# the second drum on its own steps
tapkey b1
tapkey w2
wait 40
said step 3 on
# a drum held (key 6, empty): knob 1 its hits, spread
key b5 down
wait 100
turn K1 4
wait 40
said HITS
# (steps 1 and 5 have the kick first; 9 and 13 only the lane's drum)
expect note 1 1 9 6
expect note 1 1 13 6
key b5 up
wait 40
# HOME held: a white key is a scene (a new one: a copy), and HOME's page stays
press HOME
tapkey w1
release HOME
wait 40
expect scene 2
expect page Arrange
press HOME
tapkey w0
release HOME
wait 40
expect scene 1
shot homesteps.png
